> Nah, player confronted with demon tries to make a run for it
> (controlled teleport to the upstairs, maybe?) 

If you have controlled teleport, you're pretty far in the game and also 
have the option of using level teleport; certainly what I'd try first.

If you're getting smeared badly enough by a demon lord that you have to
run for the stairs, you won't make it to the stairs.  The "meditating"
code has options for "WAITFORU" and "CLOSE", so if the demon isn't on
or next to the stairs, he won't perk up suddenly.

> and gets snuffed there.

That's pretty unlikely, seriously.  Most of the time you get a hostile
demon lord because you're near an altar and have pushed a button; those aren't 
typically generated in the same room as stairs (most common is Minetown).  
The non-altar times, you're in Gehennom, and I expect anyone in Gehennom 
to at least be somewhat prepared for an encounter with a demon lord.

> My point was that making him meditate might not be sufficient to make the
> bones "safe" (in the you only died because you were foolish enough to
> take on this thing which is too huge for you sense).

They aren't going to be 100% safe; no bones will be.  I would like it to
be far more unlikely to be unsafe than it currently is, and the
described fix would accomplish that nicely.

(There's an argument to be made that one Yeenybones in 3400 games is
"sufficiently unlikely to be not worth bothering about", too, but
regardless of that, "unlikely by comparison to 1/3400" is certainly
going to be "sufficiently unlikely".)

