This renders unexpected demon summoning (from same-race sacrifice) 
somewhat meaningless as a threat, though, if it's possible to escape
this way.  Good for bones; bad for the overall circumstance.

> I'd think this would solve your concern about the occasional
> extra-nasty bones pile while preserving your design goal of not
> letting Elbereth make most of the really tough monsters irrelevant.

It isn't a terrible idea, to be sure.  But see above; I'd still rather
have the danger tied into the critter itself, for those cases where an
out-of-depth monster is intentionally generated.

